#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""have: do we already have X?  Run it before saying something is missing.

usage: have [options] TERMS...

Each term is stemmed and expanded with synonyms ("eval harness" also looks for bench, perf,
latency, canary, probe ...). Terms that name one idea share a concept; a hit that covers more
concepts ranks higher. Five sweeps run, then one ranked report prints, with a "where to look
first" header and an exact location for every hit.

  paths      tracked file paths on each repository's default branch, grouped by directory
  scripts    package.json scripts whose name or command matches
  workflows  GitHub Actions workflows, with their state and latest run (needs the API)
  content    `git grep -i` of the typed terms on the default branch: the top 20 files that hold
             a word of every concept, by matching lines (HAVE_GREP_TIMEOUT per repository)
  boards     task lists and note directories named in the config

Repositories are read from `origin/<default branch>` after a `git fetch -q`, never from the
working tree, so a stale or sparse checkout cannot hide a file. A fetch newer than
HAVE_FETCH_TTL seconds (default 600) is reused. A checkout with no origin is read at its local
default branch and said so. "No hits" holds only for what the `searched` lines list.

options:
  --config FILE   config file (default $HAVE_CONFIG, else ~/.config/have/config)
  --root DIR      also scan the repositories under DIR (repeatable)
  --in TEXT       only repositories whose name or path contains TEXT (repeatable): drill into one
  --offline       no fetch and no GitHub API calls
  --no-fetch      read the refs as they are
  --refresh       ignore cached GitHub API answers
  --only LIST     run only these sweeps: paths,scripts,workflows,content,boards
  --skip LIST     skip these sweeps
  --limit N       rows per section (default 10)
  --jobs N        parallel repositories (default 6, or $HAVE_JOBS)
  --timeout S     stop waiting for repositories after S seconds (default 240)

config file: one `key = value` per line; `#` starts a comment at the start of a line.
  root = ~/code               scan DIR and the repositories up to `depth` levels below it
  repo = ~/src/one-repo       one checkout
  github = owner/name         a repository with no checkout here: tree and workflows by API
  gh = gh                     the GitHub CLI command (the GH environment variable wins)
  depth = 2                   levels below a root (default 2)
  exclude = */archive/*       skip checkouts whose path matches this glob
  synonyms = soak, burn-in    words that stand for one another (repeatable)
  tasks <label> = <command>   run with sh -c; prints JSON (a list of objects with id, title and
                              state) or text in which each task starts at a line that begins
                              with an id such as #12 or ABC-12
  notes <label> = <dir>       grep the .md and .txt files below it

environment: GH, HAVE_CONFIG, HAVE_FETCH_TTL, HAVE_GH_TTL (seconds a GitHub answer is reused,
default 900; --refresh overrides), HAVE_GH_BUDGET (API calls per run, default 60),
HAVE_CACHE_DIR, HAVE_JOBS.
Exit status: 0 with hits, 1 with none, 2 on a usage error.
"""
